Dear Synergya Team,

Thank you for your encouraging response and for inviting us to share more a=
bout FairBanks and the kind of partnership we would like to explore.

Please find attached our FairBanks Medical Centre Investment & Partnership =
Brief, which provides an overview of our current position, transformation v=
ision and potential partnership pathways.

About FairBanks

FairBanks Medical Centre is an operating healthcare institution in Kampala,=
 Uganda, building toward an integrated Family & Community Health Social Ent=
erprise. Our vision is to connect quality clinical and specialist care with=
 preventive healthcare, community engagement, digital health, research, inn=
ovation and more sustainable approaches to healthcare access.

Our longer-term ambition is to develop FairBanks into a leading Family & Co=
mmunity Health Social Enterprise in Uganda, with the capacity to create mea=
surable and scalable impact across communities. Our 2027=962032 roadmap foc=
uses on clinical and specialist services, preventive and community healthca=
re, digital health and community health intelligence, research and innovati=
on, inclusive healthcare financing, institutional capacity and long-term pa=
rtnerships.

What we are looking to explore with Synergya

We are particularly interested in exploring how Synergya could support Fair=
Banks to move from a promising local healthcare model toward a scalable, su=
stainable and impact-driven community health platform.

Specifically, we would welcome conversations around:

  *   Strategic scaling: advice and support on developing a scalable model =
for our community health initiatives.
  *   Partnership development: connections to organisations, institutions, =
investors and development partners that could strengthen our model.
  *   Health innovation and digital transformation: guidance, partnerships =
or technical expertise that can strengthen our digital health and community=
 health intelligence ambitions.
  *   Impact and sustainability: support in developing stronger models for =
measuring impact, financing programmes and building long-term sustainabilit=
y.
  *   Investment and growth opportunities: exploring suitable financing or =
investment partnerships for infrastructure, technology, community programme=
s and service expansion.

These areas align closely with the partnership pathways we have identified,=
 including clinical care, diagnostics and technology, digital health, commu=
nity health, research and innovation, and infrastructure and growth.

What FairBanks can offer in return

We are approaching this as a mutually beneficial strategic partnership, rat=
her than simply seeking financial support.

FairBanks can offer Synergya an opportunity to:

  *   Co-develop and test community health solutions within an operating he=
althcare environment in Uganda.
  *   Provide a practical platform for piloting innovations in community-ba=
sed healthcare, preventive services and digital health.
  *   Generate local insights and learning from implementation within under=
served urban and peri-urban communities.
  *   Contribute healthcare expertise, community relationships and implemen=
tation capacity to joint initiatives.
  *   Build a long-term partnership in Uganda and potentially East Africa a=
round scalable healthcare solutions with measurable social impact.

Our partnership philosophy is simple: =93We are not simply seeking resource=
s. We are seeking partners who want to explore what can be built together.=
=94

We would therefore be very interested in an introductory conversation with =
the Synergya team to understand your current areas of focus and explore whe=
re our respective capabilities, networks and ambitions may intersect.

Thank you again for the opportunity to introduce FairBanks. We look forward=
 to exploring what we might be able to build together.

Warm regards,
Racheal Nabukeera Sekagiri
